\section{Structural Recursion}

\begin{note}
\emph{Structural recursion} is when a class has recursive structure.
It is very common for container-like classes to use structural recursion.
\end{note}

\begin{note}
Every structurally recursive class has the same two ingredients:
\begin{enumerate}
\item a \emph{base case} for the smallest structure (often \lstinline{None}), and
\item a \emph{recursive attribute} that points to another instance of the same class.
\end{enumerate}
\end{note}
